# PiPOSS.xcodeproj is GENERATED from project.yml by XcodeGen and is not committed
# (RRR §8, T12).  `project.yml` is the only place a build setting may be edited —
# a change made in Xcode's UI is written into this bundle and the next `make`
# throws it away.  Every make target that needs the project regenerates it, so a
# fresh clone still builds with `make app-build`; the one new prerequisite is
# `brew install xcodegen` (docs/development.md).
*.xcodeproj/

# Kept from before XcodeGen: per-user Xcode state, which is never shared.  Still
# listed separately rather than folded into the line above, because that is the
# line that keeps it out if the project bundle is ever committed again.
**/xcuserdata

# SwiftPM, if a package is ever added (RRR §8).
.build/

# `scripts/release.sh` output: an archive, an export, a dmg. All regenerable, and
# leaving an app bundle here would register a second copy with LaunchServices.
build/

.DS_Store
